<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambigatus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">legendary, 6th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambigatus was a legendary king of the Bituriges in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, known from the Roman historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>. Livy says that in the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-priscus">Tarquinius Priscus</a> his people held supremacy among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a>, and that, as Gaul grew overpopulated, he sent his nephews <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellovesus">Bellovesus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segovesus">Segovesus</a> to lead migrations into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hercynian-forest">Hercynian Forest</a>.</p></div>
